{#
mail/_attachment_chip.html.twig — one attachment, with preview, download and save-to.

Extracted from _thread_message and _message_content, which carried identical
copies of the download link. The "Save to…" half is why it is shared: it needs
the user's integrations, and duplicating that lookup into two partials rendered
from five call sites is how one of them ends up stale.

The service list comes from the `integrations` Twig global rather than a
passed-in variable, because several of those call sites include with `only`.

Save-to posts a Turbo Stream and answers with a toast — no navigation, and the
thread keeps its scroll position.

Images swap the paperclip for a thumbnail. It is a separate lazy request per
attachment, so a thread full of photos costs nothing until it is scrolled to,
and a part that will not decode answers 404 — which is why the <img> removes
itself on error rather than leaving a broken-image glyph in the chip.

`download` on the link is load-bearing, not decoration. Without it Turbo Drive
intercepts the click, fetches the URL itself, finds a response that is not
HTML and drops it: the request goes out, the server answers 200 with the file,
and the browser saves nothing — a click that did nothing, with nothing in the
console to say why. Turbo leaves a link carrying `download` to the browser.
#}
{# Only the services that could actually take THIS attachment. A photo library
   drops out for a PDF — "Save to Immich" on a document is a guaranteed failure
   — while file storage stays offered for everything, unknown types included.
   The decision lives in the taxonomy (Provider::acceptsMime); here it is only
   read. #}
{% set targets = integrations.forUploadOf(part.contentType) %}
{% set hasPreview = attachment_has_preview(part) %}
{% set downloadName = part.filename ?: 'attachment' %}
{% set isPdf = attachment_is_pdf(part) %}

{#
    A PDF opens a reader instead of downloading.

    This is the ONE case where the chip's face is not an `<a download>`, and the
    note above about `download` being load-bearing still holds everywhere else:
    it is there so Turbo Drive leaves a non-HTML response alone. A button that
    opens a dialog is not a navigation, so Turbo has nothing to swallow and the
    attribute has nothing to do.

    Nothing is lost by it. The reader carries its own download link, and the
    "Save to…" half beside it is untouched.
#}
{% macro pdfFace(part, hasPreview) %}
    {# A macro gets no caller scope, so the sibling macro is imported here rather
       than passed in: an imported name lives in Twig's macro table, not in the
       context, so it cannot travel as an argument. #}
    {% import _self as chip %}
    <button type="button"
            data-controller="ui--modal"
            data-action="click->ui--modal#open"
            data-ui--modal-size-value="full"
            data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_mail_attachment_preview', { id: part.id }) }}"
            data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ part.filename ?: 'attachment.preview.untitled'|trans }}"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 {{ hasPreview ? 'p-1.5 pr-3' : 'px-3 py-2' }} text-xs
                   text-ink-soft hover:bg-hover transition-colors cursor-pointer text-left">
        {{ chip.face(part, hasPreview) }}
    </button>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro face(part, hasPreview) %}
    {% if hasPreview %}
        <img src="{{ path('app_mail_attachment_thumbnail', { id: part.id }) }}"
             alt=""
             loading="lazy"
             decoding="async"
             {# A thumbnail may legitimately not exist — see ui--broken-image.
                Was an inline onerror, which the policy refuses to run. #}
             data-controller="ui--broken-image"
             data-action="error->ui--broken-image#remove"
             class="w-8 h-8 shrink-0 rounded object-cover bg-sunken">
    {% else %}
        <i class="fa-solid fa-paperclip text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    {% endif %}
    <span class="truncate max-w-[12rem]">{{ part.filename ?: 'attachment' }}</span>
{% endmacro %}

{% import _self as chip %}

{% if targets is empty %}

    {% if isPdf %}
        <span class="inline-flex rounded-lg bg-sunken border border-line overflow-hidden">
            {{ chip.pdfFace(part, hasPreview) }}
        </span>
    {% else %}
        <a href="{{ path('app_mail_attachment', { id: part.id }) }}?download=1"
           download="{{ downloadName }}"
           class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 {{ hasPreview ? 'p-1.5 pr-3' : 'px-3 py-2' }} rounded-lg text-xs
                  bg-sunken border border-line text-ink-soft hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
            {{ chip.face(part, hasPreview) }}
        </a>
    {% endif %}

{% else %}

    {# Two boxes, not one. The rounded corners need `overflow-hidden` to clip
       the two halves inside the border — but the menu below is positioned
       past the bottom of that same box, so while the two were one element the
       menu was clipped away entirely: `hidden` came off, the element had a
       rect, and it was painted nowhere and hit-tested to whatever was behind
       it. Clicking "Save to…" opened a menu nobody could see or press, which
       is what "saving to a provider does nothing" was. Clipping now belongs to
       the inner box, positioning to the outer one. #}
    <div class="relative inline-flex" data-controller="ui--dropdown">

        <div class="inline-flex items-stretch rounded-lg bg-sunken border border-line overflow-hidden">
            {% if isPdf %}
                {{ chip.pdfFace(part, hasPreview) }}
            {% else %}
                <a href="{{ path('app_mail_attachment', { id: part.id }) }}?download=1"
                   download="{{ downloadName }}"
                   class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 {{ hasPreview ? 'p-1.5 pr-3' : 'px-3 py-2' }} text-xs text-ink-soft hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
                    {{ chip.face(part, hasPreview) }}
                </a>
            {% endif %}

            <button type="button"
                    data-action="click->ui--dropdown#toggle"
                    aria-label="{{ 'message.save_to'|trans }}"
                    class="px-2 border-l border-line text-ink-faint hover:text-ink hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-cloud-arrow-up text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </button>
        </div>

        <div data-ui--dropdown-target="menu" hidden
             class="absolute top-full mt-1 right-0 z-20 min-w-52 popover py-1">
            <p class="px-3 py-1 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint">
                {{ 'message.save_to'|trans }}
            </p>
            {# Each opens the destination picker rather than saving on the spot:
               a folder chooser for a file store, an album chooser for a photo
               library. The old one-click save to a fixed folder is now the
               "Save here" the picker lands on. A file store reopens where the
               last save landed; an album list is flat, so there is nowhere to
               reopen and it starts at the full list. #}
            {% for integration in targets %}
                {% set lastDest = integration.provider.isMediaLibrary ? null : integration.getSetting('save.last_destination') %}
                {% set browseArgs = { id: integration.id, mode: 'destination', part: part.id } %}
                {% if lastDest %}{% set browseArgs = browseArgs|merge({ folder: lastDest }) %}{% endif %}
                <button type="button"
                        data-controller="ui--modal"
                        data-ui--modal-title-value="{{ integration.name }}"
                        data-ui--modal-size-value="{{ integration.provider.isMediaLibrary ? 'full' : 'wide' }}"
                        data-ui--modal-src-value="{{ path('app_integration_browse', browseArgs) }}"
                        data-action="click->ui--modal#open click->ui--dropdown#close"
                        class="w-full flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-ink-muted
                               hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors text-left">
                    <i class="{{ integration.provider.icon }} w-4 text-center" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="truncate">{{ integration.name }}</span>
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right ml-auto text-[9px] text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </button>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>

{% endif %}
